# Backend

## Validation

Validate all external input (form submissions, API payloads, URL params) at the boundary using `zod`. Never trust data that crosses a client/server boundary.

## Authorization

Perform all authorization checks server-side (`requireCommercialMember`, `requireAnyRole`). Never rely on client-provided role or user data.

## Secrets

Environment variables with service-level access (e.g. `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`) must never be imported in Client Components or exposed to the browser.

## Route Handlers vs Server Actions

- Use Server Actions (`"use server"` in `app/actions/`) for form mutations and user-initiated writes.
- Use Route Handlers (`route.ts`, colocated or under `app/api/`) for binary downloads, webhooks, third-party callbacks, or endpoints consumed by external clients.
- Do not mix the two for the same operation.

## Supabase client boundary

- `lib/supabase/server.ts` — server client for RSC, Route Handlers, and Server Actions.
- `lib/supabase/proxy.ts` — Next.js 16 `proxy.ts` session refresh.
- `lib/supabase/admin.ts` — `server-only` service role. Never import from Client Components.
- Use `@supabase/ssr` helpers; never construct a service-role client in client code.

## Dates

Store timestamps as `timestamptz` (UTC). See `date-time.mdc` for the project-wide convention.
